# Draft knowledge entry: Boost.Math long-double promotion on HarmonyOS PC
id: DRAFT-quantlib-boost-math-long-double-promotion
trigger_tool: clang|cmake|ctest|conan
phase: compilation|testing|runtime
error_signature: boost::math::evaluation_error|halley_iterate.*root|non_central_chi_squared.*converge|series.*converge

severity: 2
category: numerical|compiler|platform|boost
match_keywords: Boost.Math, long double, BOOST_MATH_PROMOTE_DOUBLE_POLICY, halley_iterate, non_central_chi_squared, evaluation_error, HarmonyOS PC

title: Boost.Math long-double promotion can break numerical convergence on HarmonyOS PC
root_cause: HarmonyOS PC aarch64 long-double ABI and precision behavior differs from the environment assumed by some Boost.Math promotion paths. Promoting double calculations to long double can make root-finding and non-central chi-squared series evaluation fail to converge.
affected_scope: C++ scientific and financial libraries that use Boost.Math algorithms through QuantLib or similar numerical code, especially root-finding and probability-distribution paths.
verification_cmd: |
  # Confirm the failing algorithms are instantiated with long double.
  rg -n "halley_iterate|non_central_chi_squared|evaluation_error" build logs source
  # Re-run the complete upstream suite after the workaround.
  conan create archives/q/quantlib/1.43 -pr:h ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -r=ohpcd --build=missing

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: disable-boost-math-double-promotion
rec_description: Define BOOST_MATH_PROMOTE_DOUBLE_POLICY=0 in the affected Conan/CMake consumer configuration so Boost.Math keeps double calculations on the double path instead of promoting them to long double. Keep the upstream test suite enabled and verify that the full suite passes.
rec_command: |
  # Conan CMakeToolchain recipe configuration.
  tc.preprocessor_definitions["BOOST_MATH_PROMOTE_DOUBLE_POLICY"] = "0"
  # Then execute the complete upstream test suite; do not mask its exit code.
  cmake --build .
  ctest --output-on-failure
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: conan-recipe-definition

fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: isolate-platform-numerics
fallback_description: If the macro does not resolve the failure, isolate the affected numerical test and compare double versus long-double instantiations before considering a narrowly scoped upstream-compatible patch. Do not skip the complete suite without recording the exact platform limitation.
fallback_command: |
  ctest --output-on-failure
  rg -n "long double|BOOST_MATH_PROMOTE_DOUBLE_POLICY" build source
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual-diagnosis

forbid_1_pattern: test_package.*ignore|self.run.*ignore|ctest.*||true|--build.*without.*test
forbid_1_reason: The failure is numerical and must be fixed or explicitly diagnosed; suppressing the test result destroys evidence of regressions.
forbid_1_consequence: A package can appear to pass while its numerical behavior remains incompatible on HarmonyOS PC.
forbid_2_pattern: BOOST_MATH_PROMOTE_DOUBLE_POLICY.*1|BOOST_MATH_NO_LONG_DOUBLE_ROUNDING_CHECKS.*without.*test
forbid_2_reason: Re-enabling promotion or weakening numerical checks without a complete upstream test run can reintroduce the convergence failures.
forbid_2_consequence: halley_iterate and non_central_chi_squared failures may return and remain undetected.

principles:
causes:
caused_by: E127
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
